{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And he struck the hollow of his thigh.</b> The thigh-bone fixed in the hip-socket is called כַּף, because the flesh over it is like the spoon of a pot." "<b>And it was dislocated.</b> It was uprooted from its place of attachment — similar is ״פֶּן תֵּקַע נַפְשִׁי מִמֶּךָּ״ (Jeremiah 6) — a term of removal. And in the Mishnah: לְקַעְקֵעַ בֵּיצָתָן — to uproot them from the roots."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:49.738908413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}